<newsitem itemid="470701" id="root" date="1997-03-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Bridon turns to year profit.</title>
<headline>Bridon turns to year profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.1		    vs 1.5 loss</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.5		    vs 4.35</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.3		    vs 0.039 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   362		    vs 334</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had decided to pay the interim dividend as a foreign income dividend from its profitable overseas companies. It said it planned to pay the final dividend in this way. Excluding the effect of the foreign income dividend, the payout would have been 4.4 pence per share. The earnings per share figure is a headline number. Net earnings per share totalled 6.7p. Full name of the British wire, rope and industrial textiles group is Bridon Plc. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
